## **5\. Room Layout Decoder (location\_tbl)**

Rather than manually transcribing all 128 rooms, pass the raw location\_tbl byte array from knightlore.txt into this exact GDScript decoder (directly ported from retrieve\_screen) to generate all room definitions at runtime or export them to JSON.

### **5.1 Bit-Packing Format**

Each room record in location\_tbl has the structure:

> 1. room\_id (uint8): Room ID on the 16×16 grid.  
> 2. entry\_size (uint8): Number of bytes remaining in this record (including entry\_size itself).  
> 3. header (uint8):  
   * ink\_color \= header & 0x07 (ZX Spectrum bright color: 3=Magenta, 4=Green, 5=Cyan, 6=Yellow)  
   * size\_type \= (header \>\> 3\) & 0x1F (0 \= 64×64, 1 \= 32×64, 2 \= 64×32)  
> 4. **Background list:** Bytes 0..23 indexing background\_type\_tbl, terminated by 0xFF (or end of record if no foreground objects exist).  
> 5. **Foreground runs** (after 0xFF, until end of record):  
   * ctrl \= next\_byte(): count \= (ctrl & 0x07) \+ 1, block\_type \= (ctrl \>\> 3\) & 0x1F.  
   * Followed by count position bytes (pos). For each pos and each sub-sprite in block\_type\_tbl\[block\_type\]:  
     * x \= ((pos & 0x07) \* 16\) \+ ((offset & 0x01) \* 8\) \+ 72  
     * y \= (((pos \>\> 3\) & 0x07) \* 16\) \+ (((offset \>\> 1\) & 0x01) \* 8\) \+ 72  
     * z \= 128 \+ ((((pos \>\> 6\) & 0x03) \* 12 \+ offset) & 0xFC)

### **5.2 GDScript Decoder**

GDScript  
func decode\_location\_table(raw\_bytes: PackedByteArray, block\_types: Array) \-\> Dictionary:  
	var rooms: Dictionary \= {}  
	var i: int \= 0  
	while i \< raw\_bytes.size():  
		var room\_id: int \= raw\_bytes\[i\]  
		var entry\_size: int \= raw\_bytes\[i \+ 1\]  
		var record\_end: int \= i \+ 1 \+ entry\_size  
		var header: int \= raw\_bytes\[i \+ 2\]  
		var ink\_color: int \= header & 0x07  
		var size\_type: int \= (header \>\> 3\) & 0x1F

		var bg\_ids: Array\[int\] \= \[\]  
		var fg\_objects: Array\[Dictionary\] \= \[\]  
		var cursor: int \= i \+ 3

		\# 1\. Read background template IDs until 0xFF or end of record  
		while cursor \< record\_end and raw\_bytes\[cursor\] \!= 0xFF:  
			bg\_ids.append(raw\_bytes\[cursor\])  
			cursor \+= 1

		\# 2\. If 0xFF found, decode foreground object runs  
		if cursor \< record\_end and raw\_bytes\[cursor\] \== 0xFF:  
			cursor \+= 1  
			while cursor \< record\_end:  
				var ctrl: int \= raw\_bytes\[cursor\]  
				cursor \+= 1  
				var count: int \= (ctrl & 0x07) \+ 1  
				var block\_type\_id: int \= (ctrl \>\> 3\) & 0x1F  
				var template: Array \= block\_types\[block\_type\_id\]  
				for \_k in range(count):  
					if cursor \>= record\_end:  
						break  
					var pos: int \= raw\_bytes\[cursor\]  
					cursor \+= 1  
					for sub in template:  
						var off: int \= sub.offset  
						var x: int \= ((pos & 0x07) \* 16\) \+ ((off & 0x01) \* 8\) \+ 72  
						var y: int \= (((pos \>\> 3\) & 0x07) \* 16\) \+ (((off \>\> 1\) & 0x01) \* 8\) \+ 72  
						var z: int \= 128 \+ ((((pos \>\> 6\) & 0x03) \* 12 \+ off) & 0xFC)  
						fg\_objects.append({  
							"type\_id": block\_type\_id,  
							"sprite": sub.sprite,  
							"x": x, "y": y, "z": z,  
							"w": sub.w, "d": sub.d, "h": sub.h,  
							"flags": sub.flags  
						})

		rooms\[room\_id\] \= {  
			"id": room\_id,  
			"size\_type": size\_type,  
			"ink\_color": ink\_color,  
			"backgrounds": bg\_ids,  
			"foregrounds": fg\_objects  
		}  
		i \= record\_end  
	return rooms

